# Charts: an instrument, not a drawing. Rows in, axes and a crosshair out.
# Numbers are written as people write them; the chart writes them back.

scene caption
chart line | Average price of a loaf, dollars
| 2019 | $2.90
| 2020 | $3.05
| 2021 | $3.20
| 2022 | $3.85
| 2023 | $4.10
node x=2022 | The wheat shock
node y=3.5 | What a loaf used to cost
say | The price jumped in a year, then stayed.
wait 2

scene caption
chart columns | Visitors, millions
| city | visitors
| Paris | 30.4
| London | 29.1
| Rome | 21.8
| Madrid | 18.2
say aside | Hover a column for its figure.
wait 2

scene caption
chart candles approx | A coffee company's share price, dollars
| month | open | high | low | close | volume
| 2025-01 | 98 104 95 102 1.4M
| 2025-02 | 102 111 100 109 1.9M
| 2025-03 | 109 112 96 99 2.6M
| 2025-04 | 99 108 97 106 1.2M
node x=2025-03 | The frost warning
say aside | Recalled figures, not market data.
wait 2

scene caption
chart line indexed | Two economies, 2000 = 100
| year | Japan | Korea
| 2000 | 100 | 100
| 2005 | 112 | 144
| 2010 | 121 | 190
| 2015 | 130 | 234
| 2020 | 128 | 262
say | Indexed, so growth compares.
